{
  "requirement": "`habeas::validate_repository(root)` MUST return a report with the number of discovered requirements, the number of evidence files, and all validation errors for the supplied project. Ordinary invalid evidence MUST be reported in that report; an inaccessible project root MUST return an I/O error.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Implementation** (`src/evidence.rs`)\n- `validate_repository(root)` (l.119–122) returns `io::Result<EvidenceReport>` by unwrapping `inspect_repository(root)?.report`.\n- `EvidenceReport` (l.16–23) carries `requirements`, `evidence_files` and `errors`. It also carries an `examples` count. That extra field is a harmless addition. Named examples are defined and checked by `requirements.examples.evidence`, and `habeas::validate()` uses the field in its failure message.\n- `inspect_repository_with_progress` (l.170–295) computes each value:\n  - `requirements` counts only `DefinitionKind::Requirement` definitions.\n  - `evidence_files` is the number of JSON files found under `evidence/`.\n  - `errors` collects every problem found. This includes configuration errors, definition errors, evidence-file validation, orphan evidence, missing evidence, reference coverage and Rust-item coverage. Evidence and reference problems are pushed into `errors`, not returned as `Err`.\n- It starts with `fs::canonicalize(root)?`. An inaccessible or missing root therefore returns an `io::Error`, as required. Ordinary invalid evidence stays inside the report.\n- The `{impl}` marks sit on the struct, `validate_repository`, `inspect_repository` and `inspect_repository_with_progress`. These are the code that produces the report. The other `{impl}` lines on those functions belong to requirements that are assessed separately, so I found no unmarked implementing code and no unspecified behavior.\n\n**Tests**\n- `validates_full_names_requirement_text_and_input_lines` asserts the requirement count, the evidence-file count and empty errors for a valid project.\n- `collects_missing_orphan_format_false_and_changed_line_errors` checks that many kinds of invalid evidence are all reported in one report, with no `Err`. The kinds include orphan, malformed JSON, missing evidence, changed text, false determination, bad inputs and duplicate or empty definitions.\n- `inspection_progress_preserves_validation_and_finishes_each_phase` compares the counts and errors from `inspect_repository` against the progress variant, both for a clean repository and for one with broken files.\n- `inaccessible_project_root_is_an_io_error_not_a_report` checks that a missing root returns an `Err` with `ErrorKind::NotFound`, and that invalid evidence in an accessible root appears in the report instead.\n- `discovered_external_cargo_outputs_validate_freshness_and_obey_disallow` and `fixme_fixture` use the API for further scenarios.\n- `cited_example_with_a_test_and_matching_evidence_validates` (not marked `{test}` for this requirement) also asserts the example and evidence-file counts.\n\nTogether these cover the report counts, the errors collected in the report, and the I/O-error case.\n\nI found no gaps and no acknowledged FIXMEs.",
  "inputs": [
